From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 16:21:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: emit Secondary Channel Offset element during CSA

The CSA beacon is built with the old configuration, so its HT
Operation element still carries the pre-switch secondary offset,
and for 80 MHz and wider targets the ECSA operating class carries
no secondary channel information at all. Emit the Secondary Channel
Offset element in CSA beacons and probe responses; Linux mac80211
STAs parse it from any CSA-carrying frame and HT-only STAs need it
to follow a switch at 40 MHz or wider. Without it they land at
20 MHz or mis-place the secondary channel. When the puncturing
bitmap covers the secondary channel, advertise no secondary channel
instead of pointing STAs at a punctured subchannel.

802.11-2024 mandates this element in the Channel Switch
Announcement action frame for 40 MHz or wider switches (11.38.4)
and does not list it in the Beacon frame body table; STA-side
element parsing is order independent, and placement directly after
the CSA element mirrors the action frame layout. The 3 added bytes
ride the fixed slack in BEACON_TAIL_BUF_SIZE and MAX_PROBERESP_LEN.
The puncture branch is only reachable on the DFS CSA path; the
ucode switch_channel path never sets punct_bitmap.

The vendor hunk for hostapd_fill_bcn_sta_profile() was dropped; the
function only exists with the vendor MLO critical-update stack,
which this tree does not carry. The remaining beacon tail and probe
response call sites keep the helper referenced.

Based-on-work-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Based-on-work-by: Allen Ye <allen.ye@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/beacon.c |   39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/beacon.c
+++ b/src/ap/beacon.c
@@ -499,6 +499,39 @@ static u8 * hostapd_eid_csa(struct hosta
 }
 
 
+static u8 * hostapd_eid_sec_chan_offs(struct hostapd_data *hapd, u8 *eid)
+{
+#define SEC_CHAN_OFFS_BELOW	0x3
+	int sec;
+
+	if (!hapd->iconf->ieee80211n || hapd->conf->disable_11n ||
+	    is_6ghz_op_class(hapd->iconf->op_class) ||
+	    !hapd->cs_freq_params.channel)
+		return eid;
+
+	sec = hapd->cs_freq_params.sec_channel_offset;
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (hapd->cs_freq_params.punct_bitmap && sec) {
+		u32 start_freq;
+		u16 pri_ch_pos;
+		u16 sec_ch_bit_pos;
+
+		start_freq = hapd->cs_freq_params.center_freq1 -
+			(hapd->cs_freq_params.bandwidth / 2);
+		pri_ch_pos = (hapd->cs_freq_params.freq - start_freq) / 20;
+		sec_ch_bit_pos = BIT(pri_ch_pos + sec);
+		if (hapd->cs_freq_params.punct_bitmap & sec_ch_bit_pos)
+			sec = 0;
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+	*eid++ = WLAN_EID_SECONDARY_CHANNEL_OFFSET;
+	*eid++ = 1;
+	*eid++ = sec < 0 ? SEC_CHAN_OFFS_BELOW : sec;
+
+	return eid;
+}
+
+
 static u8 * hostapd_eid_ecsa(struct hostapd_data *hapd, u8 *eid)
 {
 	if (!hapd->cs_freq_params.channel || !hapd->iface->cs_oper_class)
@@ -858,6 +891,9 @@ static u8 * hostapd_probe_resp_fill_elem
 		params->csa_pos = NULL;
 	pos = csa_pos;
 
+	/* Secondary channel offset IE */
+	pos = hostapd_eid_sec_chan_offs(hapd, pos);
+
 	/* ERP Information element */
 	pos = hostapd_eid_erp_info(hapd, pos);
 
@@ -2380,6 +2416,9 @@ int ieee802_11_build_ap_params(struct ho
 		hapd->cs_c_off_beacon = csa_pos - tail - 1;
 	tailpos = csa_pos;
 
+	/* Secondary channel offset IE */
+	tailpos = hostapd_eid_sec_chan_offs(hapd, tailpos);
+
 	/* ERP Information element */
 	tailpos = hostapd_eid_erp_info(hapd, tailpos);
 
